# `deno fmt` emits LF and reports a CRLF file as "Text differed by line endings", while this
# machine's git runs with core.autocrlf=true, which hands out CRLF on every checkout. Those two
# fight each other: formatting the tree fixes `deno fmt --check` only until the next checkout
# re-introduces CRLF.
#
# Pinning eol=lf for TypeScript settles it — the blobs are stored as LF either way, so this only
# stops the checkout filter from converting them back to CRLF.
*.ts text eol=lf

# The sample reports are fixtures that the conservation check reads back byte for byte. Leave
# their line endings exactly as SkyCiv emitted them rather than letting a checkout rewrite them.
tests/HTMLFilesToBeCompiled/*.html -text
